# 0.1.18: magnetturn.sim's walk up Batalia's magnet wall, steered. From 0.1.18 the stick goes ahead in the surface's own
# plane: facing the wall square on (the head 27 degrees right of the start) is straight up it, and turning the head left
# on it takes him up and to the left. Near the wall's top (about z 41) the strip leans off to -y; the head turns left
# (to 20 degrees, 47 left of square on) and he follows it, then the stick is let go while he is still on the strip.
# QUEST_WALK_TRACE: the surface lines' "move" gains a -y part as the head turns (about -0.6 by the let-go), magnet 1 to the end;
# QUEST_STATE_TRACE: no 0x79 (slipping off) or fall (6). Not further: the strip narrows over the top and the sim's
# fixed frames land him a few tenths apart from run to run (magnetorxon.sim climbs a whole wall to its top).
